00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:20,560
like a wild eagle spotting and snatching its prey, scored the third goal.

266
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:22,270
Wild eagle...

267
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:24,810
Eagle?

268
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:31,320
Eagle Shot.

269
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:37,580
Hyuga, from today, this Eagle Shot of mine is against your Tiger Shot.

270
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:44,080
With this decisive third goal, only 5 minutes left.

271
00:15:44,330 --> 00:15:46,840
Munich's reputation is at stake.

272
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:49,800
Now Japan is making a substitution.

273
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:53,630
Morizaki-kun comes in for goalkeeper Wakashimazu-kun.

274
00:15:54,430 --> 00:15:55,590
Morizaki.

275
00:15:56,680 --> 00:16:00,020
You're a troublemaker.

276
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:05,980
You just recovered from the injury in the national tournament, leave the rest to me.

277
00:16:07,230 --> 00:16:10,610
I trust you, Morizaki, Japan's goal is in your hands.

278
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,280
Okay.

279
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:20,410
Munich team's honor is at stake, guys, get ready!

280
00:16:20,490 --> 00:16:21,410
Okay!

281
00:16:22,830 --> 00:16:24,920
Alright, everyone follow Meier.

282
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:30,420
Munich's 11 players are on the attack, this is their final effort.

283
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,840
What?

284
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,920
Guys, keep your concentration.

285
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:35,880
We know this, let's go, Kazuo.

286
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:37,550
Okay, brother.

287
00:16:39,810 --> 00:16:40,680
Move aside.

288
00:16:41,970 --> 00:16:42,930
Meier-kun got through.

289
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:46,150
He's accelerating and getting past the Tachibana brothers.

290
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:47,270
What!?

291
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:50,690
What endurance! How can they still move like that?

292
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:53,190
I'll never let you pass.

293
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:54,950
Come.

294
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:59,200
He draws in Jito-kun and Soda-kun and passes.

295
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:03,540
Japan's defense seems exhausted.

296
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,710
Alright, shoot, Meier.

297
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,130
Damn, stop him.

298
00:17:13,050 --> 00:17:13,920
Hansen.

299
00:17:14,010 --> 00:17:16,220
Meier-kun leaves the ball.

300
00:17:17,090 --> 00:17:19,970
Munich is shaking Japan's defense.

301
00:17:20,050 --> 00:17:22,220
The ball is going completely to the free Hansen-kun.

302
00:17:22,470 --> 00:17:23,720
Get it!

303
00:17:25,810 --> 00:17:29,980
Morizaki-kun, who just came in, punches it away.

304
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,360
- Morizaki. - Great catch, Morizaki.

305
00:17:32,690 --> 00:17:35,280
Helm-kun goes after the ball.

306
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,110
It's not over yet, there's still time.

307
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:38,610
Don't even think about it.

308
00:17:40,990 --> 00:17:43,830
A little showmanship doesn't hurt, let's go.

309
00:17:43,910 --> 00:17:49,120
Nitta-kun carries the ball forward, this is Japan's last counterattack.

310
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:51,130
Damn, stop them!

311
00:17:52,630 --> 00:17:54,880
- This way! - Catch.

312
00:17:55,210 --> 00:17:56,510
You can't go any further.

313
00:17:57,220 --> 00:17:58,340
Get it!

314
00:17:58,840 --> 00:17:59,840
Nice.

315
00:18:00,590 --> 00:18:02,140
Catch, Brecht.

316
00:18:03,390 --> 00:18:06,020
Take my Falcon Shot!

317
00:18:11,610 --> 00:18:16,400
Brecht-kun dives in with his life, Nitta-kun's shot hits the post.

318
00:18:16,690 --> 00:18:17,990
Damn.

319
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:33,250
The ball comes back and Tsubasa-kun flies to meet it.

320
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:41,550
And now the precious fourth goal goes into Munich's net.

321
00:18:41,890 --> 00:18:43,550
Tsubasa-senpai!

322
00:18:45,810 --> 00:18:47,770
The match ends here.

323
00:18:47,850 --> 00:18:53,310
Score 4-0. This is the Japan youth team's first victory in the European tournament.

324
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,900
W-we won!

325
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:58,360
We did it, we won!

326
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,900
This is our first victory!

327
00:18:59,990 --> 00:19:01,200
Tsubasa.

328
00:19:01,610 --> 00:19:05,950
This was Tsubasa-kun's first match for the Japan team.

329
00:19:06,030 --> 00:19:09,870
2 goals, 2 assists, involved in all key moments,

330
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:15,880
He secured the midfield against the strong Munich team with his brilliant play.

331
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:22,590
We did it. With this team, I think we can really beat the Europeans.

332
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,850
I'm glad I came to watch.

333
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,400
In the International Youth Tournament,

334
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:39,230
the only thing standing in the way of Germany's championship,

335
00:19:39,490 --> 00:19:41,990
is the Japan youth team...

336
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:46,490
and Ozora Tsubasa.

337
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,760
Nakazawa

338
00:20:02,090 --> 00:20:05,140
Sanae, bring those plates too.

339
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,720
Okay.

340
00:20:06,890 --> 00:20:08,260
Sis, sis!

341
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:11,770
They're talking about Japan youth on the sports news.

342
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:14,190
Look, there's Tsubasa-san too.

343
00:20:14,270 --> 00:20:15,270
What?

344
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:19,150
Really, Atsushi? Mom, look!

345
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:21,780
H-hey, Sanae.

346
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:27,200
Let's take a look at Japan youth's results.

347
00:20:27,530 --> 00:20:29,030
Tsubasa-kun.

348
00:20:29,030 --> 00:20:35,920
European Tournament Results

349
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:35,040
Japan youth were currently playing in the European tournament in Germany.

350
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:41,420
Their first loss was to Hamburg 6-1, their second loss to Bremen 3-2.

351
00:20:38,090 --> 00:20:44,970
Japan's dramatic game progression can't be stopped.

352
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:44,970
Initially they took consecutive defeats, but...

353
00:20:45,050 --> 00:20:47,220
Japan youth are now in the European tournament.

354
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:47,680
In the third match against Munich,

355
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:49,810
Japan's dramatic game progression can't be stopped.

356
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:51,810
They fielded Ozora Tsubasa, who joined the tournament at the last minute.

357
00:20:52,810 --> 00:20:54,060
Tsubasa-senpai!

358
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:59,610
With his play, they won 4-0 and got their first victory of the tournament.

359
00:20:59,690 --> 00:21:02,990
Honey, come quick, Tsubasa is on TV.

360
00:21:03,070 --> 00:21:04,070
Let me see.

361
00:21:04,070 --> 00:21:09,620
Japan youth won and showed their true skill and strength.

362
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:09,160
Then a 4-0 victory against Amsterdam in the Netherlands.

363
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:16,540
Japan youth won and showed their true skill and strength.

364
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:13,120
And a 3-1 victory against the Belgian youth.

365
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:17,500
Their early dominance was brilliant.

366
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:20,540
They moved completely in unity.

367
00:21:21,210 --> 00:21:23,630
Keep up your success, Tsubasa.

368
00:21:24,050 --> 00:21:26,880
And finally tomorrow,

369
00:21:26,970 --> 00:21:33,220
they arrive in Paris for their first participation in the French International Youth Tournament.

370
00:21:33,470 --> 00:21:37,190
Machiko

371
00:21:33,850 --> 00:21:37,810
Look at this! This is the captain's Eagle Shot.

372
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:40,310
Matsuyama-kun.

373
00:21:41,270 --> 00:21:47,240
Everyone is eager to see the Japan youth team's future performance.

374
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:52,410
The French International Youth Tournament,

375
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:56,250
where the best teams from around the world participate.

376
00:21:56,910 --> 00:21:58,960
The ultimate challenge has finally arrived.

377
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:06,320
Time to find out if Japanese football has reached world level.

378
00:23:46,170 --> 00:23:50,030
Reunion in Paris!!!